"title": "OráculoOposiciones · Which topics will come up in your Spanish civil-service exam",
"hero.eyebrow": "Mass civil-service exams · Official exams · Miguel Hernández University of Elche",
"hero.h1": "What the official exams say <em>about your next civil-service exam</em>",
"hero.lede": "OráculoOposiciones counts how many questions each topic has had in the official exams, estimates how many will come up in the next one and tells you how far to trust that estimate. Practise for free with official questions and the answer from the answer key, with the real structure of the exam.",
"s.empezar": "See the forecast",
"s.ejemplo": "Today's challenge",
"s.idea": "From the family of OráculoMIR and PAUsible (Fernando Borrás Rocher), adapted to civil-service exams.",
"s.j1b": "Forecast by topic",
"s.j1s": "Within each block of the exam, how many questions each topic will have, with a margin and a blind test of what it would have got right in other years.",
"s.j2b": "Mock exam with the real structure",
"s.j2s": "Official questions in the expected proportion, in the order and with the penalty of the exam. Free and with no key.",
"s.j3b": "New questions, reviewed by agents",
"s.j3s": "With your key, one agent writes and two others answer blind. Only what all three answer the same way gets through.",
"s.zl": "<li>The forecast, the mock exams and the daily challenge: computed in your browser</li><li>Your answers, your streak and your AI key</li>",
"s.zn": "<li>Only if you use the generator: the chosen topic and some official example questions</li><li>Never your data. Before the first send you see what goes out</li>",
"s.paso1": "Step 1 of 3",
